They are playing in both sides. And for this reason, those people, to befriend these people will not

01:15:34.000 --> 01:15:41.000
Edip: give you anything. You will not gain anything from them. They will not gain anything from you because really they are not sincere.

01:15:41.000 --> 01:15:42.000
Dr. Khalifa: They're being disastrous. Edip: What?

01:15:42.000 --> 01:15:45.000
Edip: Yeah, only they will give you bad ...

01:15:46.000 --> 01:15:49.000
Dr. Khalifa: Of course, you can try to help them, and guide them,

01:15:49.000 --> 01:15:57.000
but once you, you've done this, you delivered the message, you tried to help them, and then you find that they are not responding,

01:15:57.000 --> 01:16:03.000
and they continue their defiance of God and mocking you and so on. Run for your life. That is.

01:16:05.000 --> 01:16:08.000
It's a very important commandment. You will not take God's orders lightly.

01:16:09.000 --> 01:16:13.000
[3:118] O you who believe, do not befriend outsiders who never cease to wish you harm; ...

01:16:13.000 --> 01:16:17.000
etc. etc. Now, you take this seriously.

01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: Back to Dr. Sabahi and one...

01:16:26.000 --> 01:16:28.000
Dr. Sabahi: Abdullah, I think.

01:16:28.000 --> 01:16:30.000
Abdullah: I have a comment.

01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:39.000
Abdullah: The believers are recognized, the righteous people are recognized by the,

01:16:39.000 --> 01:16:51.000
by the people who don't believe in the Hereafter. And the reason they want, although they say they don't believe in what you're doing,

01:16:51.000 --> 01:17:03.000
deep inside they think you might be right. And they are scared. They want you, they want you to be in the same pot with them.

01:17:04.000 --> 01:17:15.000
And they, this, and the only way they can see is that you're wrong is something bad that happens to you,

01:17:15.000 --> 01:17:20.000
and they look forward that something will happen, bad happen to you, but it never happens.

01:17:20.000 --> 01:17:31.000
If it happens, they rejoice. If it doesn't happen, they're, they're, they are, you know, outraged inside, their inside.

01:17:31.000 --> 01:17:44.000
It's just because deep in their, in their heart, they think you might be right and they'll be in

01:17:44.000 --> 01:17:51.000
Abdullah: real trouble. And they wanna, they wanna tell you what to do the same pot, same problem.

01:17:52.000 --> 01:18:00.000
Dr. Khalifa: Abdullah is quoting 4:89, you know. Let's look at it, 4:89, it's exactly what God is telling us.

01:18:01.000 --> 01:18:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's a very good psychological analysis.

01:18:03.000 --> 01:18:04.000
A man: Page 92.

01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: Page 92, it says,

01:18:07.000 --> 01:18:12.000
[4:89] They wish that you disbelieve as they have disbelieved, then you become equal.

01:18:12.000 --> 01:18:14.000
You'll be in the same boat with them.

01:18:20.000 --> 01:18:25.000
Dr. Khalifa: It's just they feel that, I don't know, I have a feeling that they sense your soul,

01:18:25.000 --> 01:18:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: the size of your soul, it kind of bothers them. A man: Yeah. Yeah.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:32.000
Dr. Khalifa: You have a stronger soul, you go there and you take over.

01:18:34.000 --> 01:18:34.000
A man: Yes.

01:18:35.000 --> 01:18:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, they want you to be in the same boat as they are.

01:18:41.000 --> 01:18:44.000
Dr. Khalifa: Ok. 121, The Battle of Badr.

01:18:45.000 --> 01:18:48.000
Dr. Sabahi: 121, The Battle of Badr.

01:18:48.000 --> 01:18:59.000
[3:121] Recall that you (Muhammad) set out to assign to your people their positions for battle. And GOD is Hearer, Omniscient.

01:18:59.000 --> 01:19:01.000
122.

01:19:02.000 --> 01:19:08.000
[3:122] Two groups of you almost failed, and GOD was their Lord. In GOD the believers shall trust.

01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:16.000
[3:123] Thus, GOD gave you victory at Badr, even though you were weak. you shall observe GOD, to show your appreciation.

01:19:16.000 --> 01:19:23.000
[3:124] You told the believers, "Is it not enough that your Lord supports you with three thousand angels, descending?"

01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:36.000
[3:125] Yes, if you steadfastly persevere and maintain righteousness, then they attack you suddenly, your Lord will supply you with five thousand* angels, well trained.

01:19:37.000 --> 01:19:38.000
126.

01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:46.000
[3:126] GOD gives you, this good news, to assure your hearts. Victory comes only from GOD, the Almighty, Most Wise.

01:19:47.000 --> 01:19:48.000
127.

01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:55.000
[3:127] He thus annihilates some disbelievers, or neutralizes them; so they end up in failure.

01:19:56.000 --> 01:19:57.000
128.

01:19:57.000 --> 01:20:02.000
[3:128] It is not up to you; He may redeem them, or punish them for their sins.

01:20:02.000 --> 01:20:04.000
129.

01:20:04.000 --> 01:20:15.000
[3:129] To GOD belongs everything in the heavens and everything on the earth. He forgives whomever He wills, and punishes whomever He wills. GOD is Forgiver, Merciful.

01:20:15.000 --> 01:20:17.000
I stop here.

01:20:18.000 --> 01:20:27.000
121 to 129 is, as the subtitle says, is about the Battle of Badr,

01:20:27.000 --> 01:20:37.000
which, I think, or, it is the first battle that Muhammad and his followers had to fight against the disbelievers.

01:20:41.000 --> 01:20:48.000
God is reminding Muhammad that when you

01:20:48.000 --> 01:20:54.000
were assigning people in the position for battle, they knew that they are going to attack them in their town, that

01:20:54.000 --> 01:20:59.000
community that they had, and there were this bunch of, this group of

01:20:59.000 --> 01:21:09.000
believers with the prophet, and they were ready to defend. And of course, it seems that

01:21:09.000 --> 01:21:14.000
not all of those people were at the same level of belief. There were some who

01:21:14.000 --> 01:21:23.000
were better believers, they were stronger believers, and maybe there were people who had some

01:21:23.000 --> 01:21:32.000
some doubts in how far or how much God can help them. So, God is reminding Muhammad that when you

01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:42.000
were assigning your people for their positions to, to, for the battle, two groups of you almost failed,

01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:51.000
and God was their Lord. Although two groups of you failed, since I don't know the exact

01:21:51.000 --> 01:21:57.000
history of the Battle of Badr, I don't know this failure is in the real battle

01:21:57.000 --> 01:22:04.000
that they went out and fought and failed, or they failed the test, because this was a test of

01:22:04.000 --> 01:22:11.000
how much you believe. Imagine that something happens outside, you know, now we have to go

01:22:11.000 --> 01:22:20.000
and put our lives, say "okay, this is for God, and God wants us to go and fight these people who are attacking this mosque."

01:22:20.000 --> 01:22:29.000
And then, that's the real test. This is one of the most precious things that we like, is your life. You have to go and risk your life

01:22:29.000 --> 01:22:35.000
in the cause of God, you know, it is for God. So, it seems that if people have different

01:22:35.000 --> 01:22:40.000
levels of belief, some people may doubt it, say "is this real

01:22:40.000 --> 01:22:46.000
"battle? Is this really Muhammad, right, that this is for God?" And then you question.

01:22:47.000 --> 01:22:53.000
And God is saying that two groups of you almost failed in that,

01:22:53.000 --> 01:23:00.000
because you, those people didn't trust or didn't believe that God can help them with his angels.

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:03.000
And then, God is saying in 123, that

01:23:03.000 --> 01:23:06.000
[3:123] GOD gave you victory at Badr, even though you were weak. ...

01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:10.000
you know, outnumbered, weaker, maybe the other

01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:18.000
side had better arsenal. And God is reminding them that you shall observe God to, to show your

01:23:18.000 --> 01:23:20.000
appreciation. He helped you.

01:23:20.000 --> 01:23:27.000
He made you victorious over the disbelievers, and you should remember, you have to always remember God.

01:23:28.000 --> 01:23:33.000
[3:124] You told the believers, "Is it not enough that your Lord supports you with three thousand angels?"

01:23:35.000 --> 01:23:43.000
[3:125] Yes, if you steadfastly persevere and maintain righteousness, then they attack you suddenly, your Lord will supply you with five thousand angels, well trained.

01:23:44.000 --> 01:23:54.000
This clearly shows that how a believer, as Rashad just very, I think, beautifully put it, if you are believer,

01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:59.000
you have so much strength, you have something about you

01:23:59.000 --> 01:24:06.000
that even at the everyday life causes that, that, that strength.

01:24:06.000 --> 01:24:14.000
It shows in your system. You know, you walk, you talk with more strength, with self-confidence, because

01:24:14.000 --> 01:24:20.000
as was mentioned in today's Khutba. Since you believe in God,

01:24:20.000 --> 01:24:26.000
you believe in someone Who is the Superior Force, who is the Creator of the whole universe.

01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:31.000
So, you see everybody else the same. You don't worry about your boss.

01:24:31.000 --> 01:24:38.000
You don't worry about anything. You, your soul has grown so big,

01:24:38.000 --> 01:24:47.000
hopefully, that if you go in a room with some disbelievers, then there is not enough room, they just get pushed, they get squished.

01:24:47.000 --> 01:24:56.000
So, and that's the time that God comes to your help. You go in a community and you see that. This reminds me of

01:24:56.000 --> 01:25:02.000
a story that I was told, I don't know whether I told you this or not.

01:25:02.000 --> 01:25:11.000
Tariq is here. I was talking to his parents, because they are Muslims. And they were saying that the first time they were exposed to Islam,

01:25:11.000 --> 01:25:19.000
through Elijah Muhammad, in, in Brooklyn, New York, before that they were just normal people.

01:25:19.000 --> 01:25:28.000
They were always thought that, you know, they are inferior to other people and so on and so forth.

01:25:28.000 --> 01:25:35.000
But when they went through and they were introduced into what is, what was told to them that this is Islam,

01:25:35.000 --> 01:25:40.000
whatever it was, that there is a god, Allah, you have to follow Him, you believe in Him,

01:25:40.000 --> 01:25:44.000
and if you follow that, you do your Prayers, then you, you are strong.

01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:53.000
And they were saying that after they even, they got that close to the, to the real thing, which is believing in God,

01:25:53.000 --> 01:26:02.000
which then, you know, as we know the history of black Muslim movement in this country, which I'm sure

01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:11.000
Douglas is, is a better position to, to tell us about it, but the thing that was interesting

01:26:11.000 --> 01:26:16.000
to me was the strength that they said they felt with this. They said that all of a sudden

01:26:16.000 --> 01:26:21.000
they felt that God is giving them so much strength that they would go to places

01:26:21.000 --> 01:26:27.000
that they never imagined that they could go. They would go to places which were drug dealers

01:26:27.000 --> 01:26:32.000
with shotguns, you know, and they were saying that they would go to these places, and all of these

01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:37.000
nastiest people in the world that live in that area were afraid of them. Even they had

01:26:37.000 --> 01:26:46.000
shotguns, even they had knives, even whatever. And that shows, this is an example, but God

01:26:46.000 --> 01:26:53.000
is telling us exactly that if, if you believe in Him, He's gonna support you. The angels,

01:26:53.000 --> 01:26:58.000
the numbers that are given here, which in the footnote, you can see that the numbers

01:26:58.000 --> 01:27:07.000
that according the Quran are multiple of 19. God is giving these numbers and telling us that

01:27:07.000 --> 01:27:13.000
in everyday life and also in the real battles that has happened in the past, and

01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:20.000
may happen in other forms. It doesn't have to be battles that we fight with bombs and

01:27:20.000 --> 01:27:30.000
guns and so on. Everyday battle with the believers, which nowadays is mostly through, through communications,

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:33.000
then God is gonna help you to be winners.

01:27:35.000 --> 01:27:42.000
[3:126] GOD gives this you good news, to reassure your hearts. Victory comes only from GOD, the Almighty, Most Wise.

01:27:42.000 --> 01:27:47.000
This is the reassurance that God given us, the good news.

01:27:47.000 --> 01:27:52.000
[3:127] He thus annihilates some disbelievers, or neutralizes them; so they end up in failure.

01:27:54.000 --> 01:27:55.000
[3:128] It is not up to you; ...

01:27:55.000 --> 01:27:57.000
126

01:27:57.000 --> 01:28:00.000
[3:128] ... He may redeem them, or punish them for their sins.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:06.000
After you have done your work, you have done your job, it is not up to you.

01:28:06.000 --> 01:28:12.000
I don't know why always when I teach one of these verses come up, that it's not up to you.

01:28:12.000 --> 01:28:17.000
It's, He may redeem them or punish them for their sins. So, you have to do your homework,

01:28:17.000 --> 01:28:23.000
you have to do your job. The rest of it is up to God to decide what He wants to do with the disbeliever.

01:28:24.000 --> 01:28:35.000
[3:129] To GOD belongs everything in the heavens and everything on the earth. He forgives whomever He wills, and punishes whomever He wills. GOD is Forgiver, Merciful.

01:28:35.000 --> 01:28:38.000
Dr. Sabahi: I stop for discussion and questions here.

01:28:41.000 --> 01:28:45.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, I have lots to say here. Are there any questions before I say that?

01:28:45.000 --> 01:28:51.000
Ok. First of all, I urge you or encourage you to, to go to any public library

01:28:51.000 --> 01:29:01.000
and look up the Encyclopedia Britannica under Badr. B A D R. And in the Encyclopedia Britannica they give you

01:29:01.000 --> 01:29:05.000
the numbers of equipment on both sides, the disbelievers and the believers.

01:29:06.000 --> 01:29:13.000
And you can see according to those numbers from history, that the disbelievers vastly outnumbered

01:29:13.000 --> 01:29:16.000
the believers for at least ten times as much in every category.

01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:25.000
I mean seventy camels against seven, things, actually more than that. Look it up in the Encyclopedia Britannica.

01:29:25.000 --> 01:29:30.000
And then, you look at the outcome of this battle and they say that militarily,

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:39.000
it doesn't make sense. The outcome doesn't make sense. Of course, they, they couldn't count the invisible forces of the three thousand of,

01:29:39.000 --> 01:29:48.000
Dr. Khalifa: if you don't see the three thousand angels on the side of the believers. And, so, this will be quite a (unintelligible).

01:29:48.000 --> 01:29:52.000
A woman: How did they describe each side? Did they describe the believers and disbelievers? Dr. Khalifa: Yes.

01:29:52.000 --> 01:29:55.000
Dr. Khalifa: They said Muhammad side and the pagan side.

01:29:56.000 --> 01:30:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's quite fair, what I read many years ago when I read it.

01:30:01.000 --> 01:30:03.000
A man: They may have (unintelligible) by now. Dr. Khalifa: (unintelligible)

01:30:04.000 --> 01:30:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, just go and look for it in any public library, in Encyclopedia Britannica, under Badr and you'll see this.

01:30:11.000 --> 01:30:15.000
A woman: It's in the history of Islam also, the life of the prophet Muhammad.

01:30:16.000 --> 01:30:21.000
Dr. Khalifa: See, Britannica is, is a neutral, you know (unintelligible) it pretends to be neutral.

01:30:21.000 --> 01:30:32.000
But the history of Islam, we'll see they're biased. But Britannica is in a public library. Everybody reads it. It's written by

01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:36.000
the most outstanding authorities on the subject, been fully presented.

01:30:37.000 --> 01:30:44.000
The other thing I wanna say is, you notice this is specifically the time of the prophet Muhammad that was...

01:30:44.000 --> 01:30:50.000
I maintained that the time of Jihad was then, but now the battle is completely mental.

01:30:51.000 --> 01:30:59.000
However, I wanna share with you a few instances where there may be this simulation of Jihad or something.

01:30:59.000 --> 01:31:04.000
For example, in my first visit to Canada, I don't know if you still have the scar there.

01:31:08.000 --> 01:31:15.000
But there were so many threats against my life before I went, and Satan participated heavily in that

01:31:15.000 --> 01:31:22.000
to the point that I left Canada knowing that I will die there. This is the impression that I...

01:31:22.000 --> 01:31:24.000
There were very strange things happening.

01:31:25.000 --> 01:31:30.000
For example, the day before I left, I'm sitting peacefully watching the TV at home, and all of a sudden my wife says

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:32.000
"do you have insurance on your life?"

